From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:37:44 -0400
Subject: feat: site controls in page info (S-118)

Page info, opened from the site chip (toolbar T47) or the command bar's
View Site Information (commandbar K33), now holds Stedding's site
controls (docs/features/site-controls.md Si1-Si12), for a tab's page in a
normal or private tabbed window only:
- a strip with Copy link, Copy title, Mute tab, Picture in picture and
  zoom, each running the window's own command (Si2-Si5); zoom steps hold
  back Chromium's zoom bubble so the panel stays open;
- camera and microphone always listed on a page that may use them
  (https, localhost), through a new PageInfoDelegate hook (Si6);
- the session row, named by the jar the page lives in (Si7);
- Clear site data from the page's jar alone, after a question naming the
  site and the jar, taken when asked and checked again on yes; the
  embedder's storage bit stays out, so the profile-wide persistent-storage
  permission is kept (Si8);
- the dark pages switches (Si9);
- Chromium's Extensions row, opening the extensions menu, inside the page
  while the row is hidden (Si10).
Toasts 67 and 68 confirm Clear site data and Copy title.

Why: one home for a site's controls where the chip and K33 already lead,
instead of a second panel or button (BACKLOG S-118).
Removable when: never as a workaround; the hooks in page info move if
Chromium's page info gains the same controls.
